a == b (both literals): true
a == c (c is `new String(...)`): false
a.equals(c): true
a == d (d is c.intern()): true
a == e ("hel" + "lo" is constant-folded): true
a == f (prefix + "lo", built at runtime): false
a.equals(f): true

Rule of thumb: NEVER use == to compare String content.
Always use equals() (or equalsIgnoreCase()).
